# Githooks (local)
.githooks/*
# ...except the live pre-commit itself (2026-09-28): core.hooksPath points
# here, so an ignored hook is invisible enforcement, and 2026-10-11 measured
# the consequence: `git add .githooks/pre-commit` was REFUSED with "The
# following paths are ignored" (the file is tracked, force-added once), and
# that refusal sat inside an `&&` chain and staged NOTHING at all.
#
# The rule above is `.githooks/*`, NOT `.githooks/`. A trailing-slash rule
# excludes the DIRECTORY, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded -- the same rule the `state/` block below quotes -- so
# under `.githooks/` this negation did NOTHING and the hook stayed ignored
# while tracked. Excluding the CONTENTS instead lets the negation land, so the
# gate ships in a fresh clone with no force-add.
!.githooks/pre-commit
nul

