state/
backup/
renders/
reports/env_inventory/

# Evidence INSIDE state/ (2026-10-10, flaw S6). `state/` above is ignored because
# most of it is live runtime state that must never be reverted by a checkout -- but
# five of its files are the EVIDENCE for the adoption, reachability and suite
# numbers quoted in commit messages and in STRUCTURAL_FLAWS_315T.md. While they are
# ignored, a fresh clone cannot reproduce those numbers, only trust them: the same
# defect as S10 (an untracked commit gate). See EVIDENCE.md.
#
# The shape is forced by git's own rule: "It is not possible to re-include a file if
# a parent directory of that file is excluded." A bare `!state/adoption_census.json`
# therefore does NOTHING while `state/` is ignored. The directory must be
# re-included first, its contents re-excluded, and only then the files negated --
# and since the LAST matching pattern wins, this block must stay AFTER the `state/`
# rule above.
!state/
state/*
!state/adoption_census.json
!state/orphan_scan.json
!state/suite_baseline.jsonl
!state/SOLAR_PRO4_EVIDENCE_2026-10-14.jsonl
!state/SOLAR_PRO4_EVIDENCE_2026-10-14.md
# Engram lane deliverables whose whole value is the text, so they must be
# durable rather than regenerable scratch. Added 2026-10-15 with the negation
# pattern documented above (re-include the dir, re-exclude contents, then
# negate the file). #770 = intake red inventory; #793 = doc-census lane.
!state/REPORT_770_DEEPSEEK_INTAKE.md
!state/DOC_CENSUS_793_BATCH06.md
!state/DOC_DRIFT_793.md
!state/EP237_SEAM_793.md
!state/REPORT_784_DEEPSEEK_TESTCAMPAIGN.md
!state/REPORT_BYPASS_FORENSIC_2026-10-22.md
# Bake harvest lanes (RULE #714/#716 ERROR CAPTURE): the per-session JSONL is
# the encounter-time record merged by tools/merge_bake_lane.py --apply; its
# merged store and merge report stay regenerable scratch. Added 2026-10-21
# with the negation pattern documented above.
!state/bake_harvest_glm_20261021.jsonl
!state/bake_harvest_glm_2026-10-21.jsonl
# Still ignored on purpose: every other state/ file, and every SUBDIRECTORY of
# state/ (`state/*` re-excludes them as directories, and a file inside an ignored
# directory cannot be re-included). No rule here may be relaxed to `!state/**`.


# Hub-local scratch that never carried content (2026-10-07): stray file whose
# name is a single U+F0220 private-use character.
\357\200\242

# Generated work-order output: one file per source file listing
# handler line | shape | exception type | body (see tools/swallow_inventory.py).
# The CANONICAL home is state/swallow_sites/ -- the producer documents
#    python tools/swallow_inventory.py --sites state/swallow_sites
# and state/* already ignores it as a subdirectory. A run that named its output
# after a category instead (--sites unlogged_handler) left 108 regenerable files
# at the repo ROOT, where nothing ignored them: permanent git status noise, and a
# hazard for any bare git add -A. Same producer, same content, same regeneration
# command, so ignore the stray directory rather than delete or relocate it.
# Root-anchored so a legitimate nested directory of this name is unaffected.
/unlogged_handler/

# Run-output families that regenerate at the repo ROOT: basedpyright pool
# sweeps drop per-cluster *_report*.json (abl/aoa/broker/cain/cc/diskz/...
# checker outputs), run_qanalysis*.py writes analysis_logs/ (dlq_*.json,
# q_table*.npy), _evo_graph_build.py writes EVOLUTION_CALLGRAPH.svg/.mmd,
# ad-hoc tree censuses write _tree.json. Same rationale as the unlogged_handler
# case - produced by a documented command, so ignore at root, don't delete.
# Root-anchored so nested namesakes are unaffected.
/*_report*.json
/_tree.json
/EVOLUTION_CALLGRAPH.svg
/EVOLUTION_CALLGRAPH.mmd
/analysis_logs/
/.pmb/

